mindmap
root((the documentation update))
  what has to be documented
    what shipped since the README was written
    the codes this work added
      7 of 7 are in neither README
      a reader of the README cannot look one up
    the reference material is English only
      the bilingual rule applies to shipped text
  where each fact belongs
    the README pair tells the human story
      a capability gets a sentence and its non-goal
    a reference file carries the domain detail
      the code table for its family
    the memory carries the decisions
      and why the alternative was rejected
    one fact lives in one place
      everything else points at it
  the references section
    extracted from the provenance tables
      not rewritten from memory
        a hand-copied citation drifts from its source
        a scan that truncates a publisher invents a work
    grouped by where the method is used
      verification and model checking
      data, structure and diagrams
      external checkers the plugin translates into
    each entry says which file cites it
      a reader can check the claim in place
    and what is NOT published is named as such
      most checks here are house conventions
        saying so is the point of the distinction
  how the update is kept true
    the maps are regenerated, never hand-drawn
      four of them now, each with a drift test
    a claim about the repository is checked against it
      counts, links, gates and citations
    a document that names a capability names where it lives
  what this update is not
    not a rewrite of the README
      it adds what is missing and leaves the rest
    not a second copy of the reference tables
      the references section points, it does not duplicate
